Package: ForestFireR
Type: Package
Title: Spatial and Mean-Field Forest-Fire Invasion Model
Version: 0.3.0
Author: Rebeca de la Fuente, Leonardo A. Saravia
Maintainer: Leonardo A. Saravia <lasaravia@untdf.edu.ar>
Description: R/Rcpp interface to the spatial stochastic (Gillespie) and
    deterministic mean-field forest-fire invasion model described in
    "Dynamics of invasion in forest-fire models". Provides R-friendly
    functions, using the paper's own notation (xi, eta, p), to generate
    initial landscapes, run spatially-explicit and well-mixed simulations
    with full trajectory/snapshot recording, and reproduce the paper's
    figures. Based on the original forest_fire_model.cpp engine, with
    missing grid-index-mapping functions restored, dynamic grid sizing,
    reproducible RNG seeding, and a numerically stable mean-field
    integrator added.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp
LinkingTo: Rcpp
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
NeedsCompilation: yes
